        "original_id": "dd05e7f0-8e56-5050-9656-23ad0f0e6cb7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Carroll County, Ohio\n- People: Charles Carroll of Carrollton, Doc Watson, Jeff Pfeffer, Bill Schardt, Jack Zalusky\n- Organizations: La Crosse Blackhawks\n- Roles: Declaration of Independence signer, Major League Baseball pitcher\n- Topics: Naming origins, Catholic signatories, baseball careers\n\nFacts:\n- Carroll County, Ohio, is named for Charles Carroll of Carrollton.\n- Charles Carroll of Carrollton was the last surviving signer of the Declaration of Independence.\n- Charles Carroll of Carrollton was the only Catholic signatory of the Declaration of Independence.\n- Doc Watson was born on January 30, 1886, in Carroll County, Ohio.\n- Charles John \"Doc\" Watson was a pitcher in Major League Baseball.\n- Doc Watson died on December 30, 1949, in San Diego, California.\n- Jeff Pfeffer, Bill Schardt, Doc Watson, and Jack Zalusky played for the La Crosse Blackhawks.",
